                   JEOLast v1.22b - by Jan Erik Olausen
                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  JEOLast generates an ANSI-file over the last specified # of callers.

  Here's what to do:

  JEOLast 1,2 PREMIERE 15 Bulletins:NEWS1 50B ABBS: "Jan_Erik Olausen"

  Where:
               1,2.... = Node number (1 - 99). 0 = From all nodes.
                         JEOLast doesn't include local logins as default,
                         but it can be switched on (see below)

              PREMIERE = Name of your grabfile without extention.

                    15 = # of last callers to display (1 - 15).
                   15L = Shows locale logins as well.

       Bulletins:NEWS1 = Where to store the generated ANSI-file.

                    50 = How much kilobytes JEOLast shall read from each
                         logfile. Must be from 30 to 150.
                   50B = Line gets BOLD if the baud rate are > 28800.
                   
                 ABBS: = Path of where to find the logfiles.

    "Jan_Erik Olausen" = Doesn't show this user on extern logins.
                         NOT REQUIRED. Don't use this option if you NEVER
                         call your BBS. Because you can't see if somebody
                         else was calling in your name.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  That's all...
  Almost :-)

  ABBS:Sys/Logout.script could look like this with 2 nodes:
  ---------------------------------- CUT ----------------------------------
  .key param
  .bra {
  .ket }

  Run ABBS:Utils/JEOLast 1,2 PREMIERE 15 Bulletins:NEWS1 50B ABBS:
  ---------------------------------- CUT ----------------------------------

	If you want to display if a user is ONLINE, do as follows:

  The beginning of 'ABBS:Sys/Loginscript.abbs' MUST be:
  ---------------------------------- CUT ----------------------------------
	/*********** Hmmm. This dummy line has to be here ;-) ****************/

  Options results
  NODENUMBER; node=RESULT
  Address Command 'Execute ABBS:sys/login.script 'node''

  /* Rest of the script */
  ---------------------------------- CUT ----------------------------------
  Where 'ABBS:sys/login.script' are the same as my 'ABBS:sys/logout.script'
  ==========================================================================

  Versions:
  ~~~~~~~~~
  (25.08.97) v1.22b - Fixed bug in 'Time used'
  (13.08.97) v1.22a - There was a bug when a user uploaded or downloaded a
                      grab different from a QWK-grab. Silly bug now fixed.
                      Changes some code for more exact output.
                      The optional bold text when baud rate >= 28800 is
                      changed to > 28800.
  (25.10.95) v1.22  - If the baud rate >= 28800 the the hole line is BOLD.
                      SysOp has to turn this feature on.
  (08.10.95) v1.21  - The new user flag is now set even when ABBS dosn't
                      find the text/postloginfile.
  (24.09.95) v1.20  - Fixed bug in text if your computer crashed. Fixed bug
                      when 'all nodes' was on and the path to your logfiles
                      was other than ABBS:. Changed text colours in
                      'C R A S H E D' different from 'O N L I N E' :-)
  (05.09.95) v1.19  - Shows if the machine has crached when a user was
                      online. ANSI-output is over 25% smaller and faster.
                      Fixed bug in 'Changed name'.
  (26.08.95) v1.18  - Removed automatic '.ansi' extention. ABBS only updates
                      text-bulletins.
  (24.08.95) v1.17  - Different colour for each node. Added kilobytes to read
                      from each logfile and the path to the logfiles.
                      Speed >= 28800 is bold. Shows local logins if
                      <# of last callers> ends with a 'L', 15L.
  (16.08.95) v1.16  - Adds .ansi extention to file name. Reads 80 KB of each
                      logfile instead of 50 KB.
  (13.08.95) v1.15  - 'Resigned conf' replaced with 'Changed name'. Fixed
                      small bug when SysOp extern login was turned on.
                      Cleaned up findstuff routines so JEOLast is now as fast
                      as it can be :-) Changed output a bit.
  (11.08.95) v1.14  - Now you can select which node to include: 1,2,6,8 etc.
                      JEOLast now reads only the last 50 KB from the logfile.
                      Should be enough for the last 15 callers :-)
  (10.08.95) v1.13  - Fix multi-node bug when a user was online or local.
                      Optimized routines. Now shows when a user is online.
  (09.08.95) v1.12  - Added 'Exited to DOS', 'Resigned conf'. Splitted file-
                      search and keyword-search. Just for fun :-)
                      Added a center-text routine to the header-text.
  (08.08.95) v1.11  - If node argument is 0 then JEOLast scans all logfiles.
                      Fixed Enforcer Hit if 'Sysop's name' wasn't in argument
  (07.08.95) v1.10  - Doesn't show local logins. Doesn't show sysop's extern
                      logins (not required). Added 'Killed msg'
  (06.08.95) v1.09  - Added protocoll, V = V42BIS, M = MNP. If filename is *
                      then the output goes to the screen.
  (29.07.95) v1.08  - Replaced 'Exited to DOS' to 'Thrown out'.
                      Added [] again. :-)
  (26.07.95) v1.07  - Fixed 'Error in logfile' when ABBSs logfile len > 70. 
  (23.07.95) v1.06  - Fixed bug in 'Keyword search'. 
  (23.07.95) v1.05  - Added 'scanned' as keyword search. When the logfile
                      was missing 'time used' JEOLast used the last users
                      time, now fixed.. Changed 'S' to 'X'
  (22.07.95) v1.04  - Fixed line > 70 chars bug in ABBS logfile. Fixed
                      'Uploaded' when grabbed. A ! was missing :-)
                      Added 'Exited to DOS'
                      Added 'Keyword Search'
                      Added 'Failed Download'
                      Added 'Failed Upload'
                      Added 'Replied'
                      Added 'Left Comment'
                      Added 'Bulletin Read'
                      You can have as many as 999 last callers now °-)
                      Cleaned up the output a bit :-)
  (21.07.95) v1.03  - Fixed 'Replied' W flag. Fixed 'upload' flag if grabbed
  (21.07.95) v1.02  - Added 'Misc command' and 'Fell asleep'
  (19.07.95) v1.01  - Fixed 'Paged SysOp' P flag 
  (19.07.95) v1.00  - First release. No known bugs

